\DOC GLOBALIZE_PRECONDITION_TAC

\TYPE {GLOBALIZE_PRECONDITION_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
On a goal whose conclusion is an {ensures} triple, moves state-independent
conjuncts of the precondition out into the goal's assumption list.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. The conclusion must be an {ensures} statement whose
precondition is a lambda over a state variable. Every top-level conjunct of
that precondition that does not depend on the state variable — including
implications, existentials, inequalities and equations between program
variables — is deleted from the precondition and added as a new assumption at
the end of {A}; parenthesised groupings of conjuncts that are touched are
flattened. The postcondition and frame are unchanged. More than one conjunct
may be lifted at once, each becoming a separate assumption.
{
       A ?- ensures ... (\s. t /\ u) post frame
     ========================================== GLOBALIZE_PRECONDITION_TAC
       A, t ?- ensures ... (\s. u) post frame
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces the inputs are {ensures} goals that already carry a list
of assumptions, and the tactic always produces this single transformed goal.

\ENDDOC
